WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.160
Joe: If someone has an autistic
child or children, they can find

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.310
that their extended family and
friends, can become key parts of

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.930
their informal support network.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.120
This is made easier when family and
friends become aware of a child’s

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.300
autism diagnosis at an early stage,
and makes it easier for them to

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.050
understand any issues, what it
means and how it affects the family.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.990
Beth: Parents of children with
autism should first relay basic

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.809
information to their potential
informal support network about autism

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.639
and how it affects their child.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:35.280
Extended family and friends will
probably respond in different ways to a

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.800
child’s autism diagnosis and behaviour.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.629
Some might be ready to offer
support straight away, however

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.980
others might take a bit longer
to understand how they can help.

00:00:45.679 --> 00:00:49.530
Some family and friends might find
it hard to give support or they might

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.700
respond in ways that aren’t very helpful.

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:55.069
Joe: It is important that people
acknowledge the feelings of

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.470
family and friends as they might
be having trouble understanding

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.239
the diagnosis and what it means.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:03.889
It’s important for anyone relying
on family and friends to make them

00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:08.209
aware of how autism affects their
child’s behaviour, for example, the

00:01:08.219 --> 00:01:11.820
child may sometimes get overwhelmed
and needs quiet time on their own.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:16.590
Beth: Someone offering informal support
needs to be told how best to connect

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:20.530
with the child, their likes and dislikes,
and the best ways to communicate.

00:01:21.179 --> 00:01:24.649
Extended family get-togethers and
activities that suit the child’s

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.909
needs and abilities, could be
organised to facilitate this.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:32.690
Joe: Unhelpful reactions usually happen
because people aren’t sure how to respond,

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:35.270
don’t understand or feel uncomfortable.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:40.119
Telling close friends and family about
a child's autism diagnosis can help them

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:44.989
understand what this means and opening
up about what help and support the

00:01:45.039 --> 00:01:47.220
whole family needs can be beneficial.

00:01:47.959 --> 00:01:51.720
Beth: They may be able to help with
everyday things, so parents have more time

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:57.820
to focus on themselves or their child or
offer emotional support in times of need.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.030
Other groups that can help are
national charities, and it may help

00:02:01.039 --> 00:02:04.590
by listening to or reading other
people's experiences of autism online

00:02:04.799 --> 00:02:06.759
and joining local support groups.

00:02:07.139 --> 00:02:11.950
Joe: There are many people with experience
of autism either directly or indirectly

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.600
offering support and sharing their
stories on forums and social media.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.589
People don’t have to have to talk to
others in online groups, but it can be

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.100
helpful to look at what they're saying.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.100
Beth: Comments on social media and
forums are often based on personal

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.330
experience and should not be taken purely
as advice, but could be more help as a

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.360
source of experience based knowledge.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:37.070
National charities such as National
Autistic Society have Facebook, Twitter

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.609
and online communities can also be
looked at as possible areas of support.

